From b7b4b81b56cc07df1f8cd328e0cc1971b64b368d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kalesh Singh <kaleshsingh@google.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 07:25:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ANDROID: 16K: Fix potential lock inversion deadlock in
 linker_ctx()

When madvise(MADV_DONTNEED) executes under a per-VMA read lock, it
holds the VMA's vm_refcnt. If linker_ctx() is called in this context
and lock_vma_under_rcu() fails, it currently falls back to acquiring
mmap_read_lock(). This inverts the lock order, as the correct order
is mmap_lock -> per-VMA lock.

If a concurrent thread executes a VMA write operation (such as
mprotect), it acquires mmap_write_lock and waits for the target VMA's
vm_refcnt to drain. If linker_ctx() is waiting for mmap_read_lock at
the same time, both threads enter an unkillable deadlock.

Thread A (madvise)                   Thread B (mprotect)
------------------                   ------------------
Acquire VMA read lock (vm_refcnt++)
  |
  |                                  Acquire mmap_write_lock
  |                                  Acquire VMA write lock
  |                                  (Wait for vm_refcnt -> 0)
  |                                            |
linker_ctx() starts                            |
lock_vma_under_rcu() fails                     |
Acquire mmap_read_lock (fallback)              |
(Wait for mmap_lock)                           |
  |                                            |
  v                                            v
[Blocked on B]                               [Blocked on A]

To resolve this, the mmap_lock fallback is removed from linker_ctx().
If lock_vma_under_rcu() fails, the function now conservatively
returns false. This is safe as it only affects best-effort
/proc/*/[s]maps emulated output.

Additionally, early checks are added to reject kernel threads and
non-user mode contexts immediately since they cannot be the dynamic
linker.

Bug: 508702921
Change-Id: Ie2801be089df68a22f10cfdb8c3fa390c1da7177
Signed-off-by: Kalesh Singh <kaleshsingh@google.com>
(cherry picked from commit 099fe093d60d64b11b956622feb29bbfcf6b4c7e)
---
 mm/pgsize_migration.c | 41 +++++++++++++++++------------------------
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 24 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mm/pgsize_migration.c b/mm/pgsize_migration.c
index 217f44ee1165..97e6c2d35021 100644
--- a/mm/pgsize_migration.c
+++ b/mm/pgsize_migration.c
@@ -223,36 +223,29 @@ static inline bool linker_ctx(void)
 	struct vm_area_struct *vma;
 	struct file *file;
 
-	if (!regs)
+	/*
+	 * Called from madvise_dontneed_single_vma() with the target VMA
+	 * read-locked (MADVISE_VMA_READ_LOCK).  We MUST NOT take mmap_lock
+	 * here: that inverts the mmap_lock -> per-VMA-lock order and ABBA-
+	 * deadlocks against a concurrent vma_start_write() on the target
+	 * may occur.
+	 *
+	 * io_wq workers / kthreads have zeroed pt_regs (pc==0) and are never
+	 * the dynamic linker, so reject them up front instead of falling back
+	 * to mmap_read_lock().
+	 */
+	if (!regs || current->flags & (PF_IO_WORKER | PF_KTHREAD) ||
+	    !user_mode(regs))
 		return false;
 
 	vma = lock_vma_under_rcu(mm, instruction_pointer(regs));
 
 	/*
-	 * lock_vma_under_rcu() is a try-lock that can fail if the
-	 * VMA is already locked for modification.
-	 *
-	 * Fallback to finding the vma under mmap read lock.
+	 * Conservatively reject; only affects /proc/<pid>/[s]maps emulated
+	 * output.
 	 */
-	if (!vma) {
-		mmap_read_lock(mm);
-
-		vma = find_vma(mm, instruction_pointer(regs));
-
-		/* Current execution context, the VMA must be present */
-		BUG_ON(!vma);
-
-		/*
-		 * We cannot use vma_start_read() as it may fail due to
-		 * false locked (see comment in vma_start_read()). We
-		 * can avoid that by directly locking vm_lock under
-		 * mmap_lock, which guarantees that nobody can lock the
-		 * vma for write (vma_start_write()) under us.
-		 */
-		down_read(&vma->vm_lock->lock);
-
-		mmap_read_unlock(mm);
-	}
+	if (!vma)
+		return false;
 
 	file = vma->vm_file;
 	if (!file)
-- 
2.55.0

